==Recurring Pokémon that have been caught==
Thirty-one recurring wild Pokémon were {{pkmn2|caught}}: twelve by {{Ash}}, one by {{an|Lance}}, one by {{an|Clemont}}, one by [[Jessie]], one by {{an|Lana}}, one by [[Acerola]], two by [[James]], three by [[Goh]], two by [[Liko]], four by [[Roy]], two by [[Dot]], and one by [[Amethio]].

* In ''[[EP003|Ash Catches a Pokémon]]'', Ash caught a {{p|Caterpie}} that he started to battle in the [[EP002|previous episode]]. It was eventually released as a {{AP|Butterfree}} in ''[[EP021|Bye Bye Butterfree]]''.
* After Ash released his {{AP|Lapras}} in ''[[EP113|Viva Las Lapras]]'', it has since reappeared twice as a wild Pokémon, once in ''[[EP257|Lapras of Luxury]]'' and again in ''[[JN143|Ride, Lapras, Ride!]]''.
* In ''[[EP236|Rage of Innocence]]'', {{an|Lance}} caught the {{TP|Lance|red Gyarados|Gyarados}}, which was causing a rampage at the [[Lake of Rage]] in the [[EP235|previous episode]].
* In ''[[AG182|Channeling the Battle Zone!]]'', Ash caught the {{AP|Aipom}} that had been following him since ''[[AG179|Slaking Kong!]]''. She had a habit of taking [[Ash's hat]] from him making him chase her around, sometimes lowering her eyelid and sticking out her tongue at him when he tried to get it back. She was eventually traded to {{an|Dawn}} in ''[[DP055|Throwing the Track Switch]]'' and evolved into an Ambipom in ''[[DP060|Journey to the Unown!]]'' under her care.
* In ''[[DP157|Gotta Get a Gible!]]'', Ash caught the {{AP|Gible}} that had been following him since the [[DP156|previous episode]], after he helped him learn {{m|Draco Meteor}}.
* In ''[[BW065|Battling the Bully!]]'', Ash caught the {{AP|Sunglasses Krokorok|Krokorok}} (which debuted as a Sandile) that had been following him since ''[[BW003|A Sandile Gusher of Change!]]''. He evolved into a Krookodile in ''[[BW092|Ash, Iris, and Trip: Then There Were Three]]'', during his battle against [[Iris's Dragonite]].
* After Ash released his {{AP|Greninja}} in ''[[XY139|Facing the Needs of the Many!]]'', it has since reappeared multiple times as a wild Pokémon.
* In ''[[XY004|A Shockingly Cheeky Friendship!]]'', Clemont caught the {{TP|Clemont|Dedenne}} that had been following {{an|Bonnie}} since the [[XY003|previous episode]], and gave it to her to take care of.
* After Ash released his {{AP|Goodra}} in ''[[XY070|Beyond the Rainbow!]]'', it has since reappeared multiple times as a wild Pokémon.
* In ''[[SM004|First Catch in Alola, Ketchum-Style!]]'', Jessie caught a {{TP|Jessie|Mimikyu}} after it helped {{TRT}} attack Ash and {{AP|Pikachu}} in the [[SM003|previous episode]]. After its release in ''[[SM146|Thank You, Alola! The Journey Continues!]]'', it has since reappeared multiple times as a wild Pokémon.
* After James released his {{TP|James|Mareanie}} in ''[[SM146|Thank You, Alola! The Journey Continues!]]'', she has since reappeared multiple times as a wild Pokémon.
* In ''[[SM015|Rocking Clawmark Hill!]]'', Ash caught the {{AP|Rockruff}} that lived with him and {{an|Professor Kukui}} in Kukui's home since ''[[SM002|The Guardian's Challenge!]]''. Although Kukui took care of it, it was never actually his Pokémon. It evolved into a {{DL|List of Pokémon with form differences|Lycanroc|Dusk Form}} {{AP|Lycanroc}} in ''[[SM037|Rising from the Ruins!]]''.
* In ''[[SM021|One Journey Ends, Another Begins...]]'', Ash caught the {{AP|Litten}} that often wandered around [[Melemele Island]] since ''[[SM001|Alola to New Adventure!]]''. It evolved into a Torracat in ''[[SM063|Pushing the Fiery Envelope!]]''. It later evolved into an Incineroar in ''[[SM143|Fiery Surprises!]]''.
* In ''[[SM067|Love at First Twirl!]]'', Ash caught the {{AP|Poipole}} that often wandered around [[Melemele Island]] since ''[[SM061|A Mission of Ultra Urgency!]]''. He released it back into the wild in ''[[SM090|Securing the Future!]]''.
* In ''[[SM099|We Know Where You're Going, Eevee!]]'', {{an|Lana}} caught the {{p|Eevee}} that had traveled across the sea to [[Alola]] from ''[[SM093|Lillier and the Staff!]]'' to ''[[SM096|Don't Ignore the Small Stufful!]]''. She gave him the [[nickname]] [[Sandy]].
* In ''[[SM112|Got Meltan?]]'', Ash caught the {{AP|Meltan}} that befriended {{AP|Rowlet}} in the [[SM111|previous episode]]. In ''[[SM138|Final Rivals!]]'', it evolved into {{p|Melmetal}}.
* In ''[[SM131|The Battlefield of Truth and Love!]]'', [[Acerola]] was revealed to have caught the {{pkmn2|Totem}}-sized {{p|Gengar}} nicknamed Greedy Rapooh, which she tried to help in ''[[SM073|Why Not Give Me a Z-Ring Sometime?]]''.
* In ''[[JN005|Mind-Boggling Dynamax!]]'', [[Goh]] caught the {{p|Scorbunny}} that had been following him since the [[JN004|previous episode]]. In ''[[JN017|Kicking It from Here Into Tomorrow!]]'', it evolved into {{p|Raboot}}. Later in ''[[JN045|Sword and Shield... The Legends Awaken!]]'', it evolved into {{TP|Goh|Cinderace}}.
* In ''[[JN016|A Chilling Curse!]]'', Ash caught the {{AP|Gengar}} that haunts the [[Cerise Laboratory]] since ''[[JN011|Best Friend...Worst Nightmare!]]''.
* In ''[[JN028|Sobbing Sobble!]]'', Goh caught the {{TP|Goh|Sobble}} that had been following him since the [[JN027|previous episode]].
* In ''[[JN045|Sword and Shield... The Legends Awaken!]]'', Goh caught the {{TP|Goh|Eternatus}} that appeared in ''[[JN012|Flash of the Titans!]]''.
* In ''[[JN070|Take My Thief! Please!]]'', James caught the {{TP|James|Morpeko}} that had been following him since ''[[JN028|Sobbing Sobble!]]''.
* In ''[[HZ006|The Ancient Poké Ball]]'', Roy caught the {{TP|Roy|Fuecoco}} that first appeared in ''[[HZ002|The Pendant That Starts It All (Part Two)]]''.  He evolved into a {{p|Crocalor}} in ''[[HZ067|Shine on, Terastallization! Liko vs. Roy!]]''. He later evolved into an {{p|Skeledirge}} in ''[[HZ119|Don't Give Up, Crocalor!]]''.
* In ''[[HZ014|Fly! Wattrel!!]]'', Roy caught the {{TP|Roy|Wattrel}} that first appeared in ''[[HZ013|An Unexpected Picnic!]]''. It evolved into a {{p|Kilowattrel}} in ''[[HZ052|Wattrel's High Wind Warning!]]''.
* In ''[[HZ016|Quaxly, We Can Do It]]'', Dot caught the {{TP|Dot|Quaxly}} that first appeared in ''[[HZ001|The Pendant That Starts It All (Part One)]]''. He evolved into a {{p|Quaxwell}} in ''[[HZ059|Dance, Quaxly! The Blue Medali Step!]]''. He later evolved into a {{p|Quaquaval}} in [[HZ128]].
* In ''[[HZ075|The Wonders of the World!]]'', Liko caught the {{p|Terapagos}} that first appeared in ''[[HZ002|The Pendant That Starts It All (Part Two)]]'', nicknaming it [[Pagogo]]. It was eventually released in [[HZ136]].
* In ''[[HZ102|The Knight in the Ruins]]'', Liko caught the {{TP|Liko|Charcadet}} that first appeared in ''[[HZ057|The Terapagos I Don't Know]]''. It evolved into an {{p|Armarouge}} in [[HZ124]].
* In ''[[HZ105|Riding the Waves]]'', Dot caught the {{TP|Dot|Gimmighoul}} that first appeared in ''[[HZ057|The Terapagos I Don't Know]]''. It evolved into a {{p|Gholdengo}} in ''[[HZ120|Dot and Penny's Top-Secret Mission!]]''.
* Chronology, [[Roy's Lucario]] first appeared in ''[[HZ112|Mega Evolution - Roy]]''. It was later caught in ''[[HZ114|Mega Evolution - Bonds]].
* In [[HZ125]], [[Amethio]] was revealed to have caught the [[White Zygarde]], which belonged to his grandfather, [[Gibeon]], in ''[[HZ045|From So Far Away]]''. It was eventually released in [[HZ136]].
* In [[HZ129]], Roy caught the [[Black Rayquaza]], which belonged to [[Lucius]], in ''[[HZ006|The Ancient Poké Ball]]''. It was later released in [[HZ136]].

